	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:03,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3980
			},
			"text": " This question comes from Trevor, who asks, \"If all the lightning that occurs worldwide"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,980",
				"to": "00:00:10,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3980,
				"to": 10460
			},
			"text": " on any given day all struck in the same place at once, what would happen to that place?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:10,460",
				"to": "00:00:13,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 10460,
				"to": 13400
			},
			"text": " They say lightning never strikes in the same place twice."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:13,400",
				"to": "00:00:17,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 13400,
				"to": 17060
			},
			"text": " They are wrong, and it's a little surprising that this saying has survived."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:17,060",
				"to": "00:00:19,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 17060,
				"to": 19940
			},
			"text": " You'd think people who believed it would have been gradually filtered out."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,940",
				"to": "00:00:23,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19940,
				"to": 23020
			},
			"text": " People often wonder whether we could harvest electrical power from lightning."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:23,020",
				"to": "00:00:24,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 23020,
				"to": 24820
			},
			"text": " On the face of it, it makes sense."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:24,820",
				"to": "00:00:28,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 24820,
				"to": 28360
			},
			"text": " After all, lightning is electricity, and lightning strikes seem pretty powerful."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:28,360",
				"to": "00:00:32,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 28360,
				"to": 32260
			},
			"text": " The problem is, a lightning strike is over so fast that the total amount of energy delivered"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:32,260",
				"to": "00:00:35,860"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 32260,
				"to": 35860
			},
			"text": " isn't that extreme, and in any case, it's very hard to get lightning to strike where"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,860",
				"to": "00:00:36,860"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35860,
				"to": 36860
			},
			"text": " you want it."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:36,860",
				"to": "00:00:40,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 36860,
				"to": 40460
			},
			"text": " A typical lightning strike delivers enough energy to power a residential house for about"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:40,460",
				"to": "00:00:41,500"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 40460,
				"to": 41500
			},
			"text": " two days."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:41,500",
				"to": "00:00:44,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 41500,
				"to": 44740
			},
			"text": " That means that even the Empire State Building, which is struck by lightning about 100 times"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:44,740",
				"to": "00:00:48,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 44740,
				"to": 48560
			},
			"text": " a year, wouldn't be able to keep a house running on lightning power alone."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:48,560",
				"to": "00:00:51,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 48560,
				"to": 51360
			},
			"text": " Even in regions of the world with a lot of lightning, such as Florida and the eastern"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:51,360",
				"to": "00:00:55,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 51360,
				"to": 55240
			},
			"text": " Congo rainforest, the power delivered to the ground by sunlight outweighs the power delivered"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:55,240",
				"to": "00:00:57,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 55240,
				"to": 57600
			},
			"text": " by lightning by a factor of a million."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:57,600",
				"to": "00:01:01,180"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 57600,
				"to": 61180
			},
			"text": " This makes sense, because ultimately, lightning is powered by sunlight."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:01,180",
				"to": "00:01:05,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 61180,
				"to": 65260
			},
			"text": " Generating power from lightning is kind of like building a wind turbine powered by tornadoes."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:05,260",
				"to": "00:01:06,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 65260,
				"to": 66260
			},
			"text": " Impractical."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:06,260",
				"to": "00:01:08,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 66260,
				"to": 68460
			},
			"text": " Although that would also be very cool."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:08,460",
				"to": "00:01:11,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 68460,
				"to": 71460
			},
			"text": " In Trevor's scenario, all the lightning hits the world in one place."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:11,460",
				"to": "00:01:13,860"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 71460,
				"to": 73860
			},
			"text": " That would make power generation a lot more attractive."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,860",
				"to": "00:01:16,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73860,
				"to": 76900
			},
			"text": " By happening in the same place, let's assume that the lightning bolts all come down in"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:16,900",
				"to": "00:01:19,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 76900,
				"to": 79020
			},
			"text": " parallel right up against each other."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:19,020",
				"to": "00:01:22,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 79020,
				"to": 82260
			},
			"text": " The main channel of a lightning bolt, the part that's actually carrying current, is"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:22,260",
				"to": "00:01:24,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 82260,
				"to": 84140
			},
			"text": " about a centimeter or two in diameter."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:24,140",
				"to": "00:01:27,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 84140,
				"to": 87700
			},
			"text": " Our bundle contains about a million separate bolts, which means it'll be about six meters"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:27,700",
				"to": "00:01:31,340"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 87700,
				"to": 91340
			},
			"text": " in diameter, hitting a region of the ground the size of the center circle of a basketball"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:31,340",
				"to": "00:01:32,340"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 91340,
				"to": 92340
			},
			"text": " court."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:32,340",
				"to": "00:01:36,100"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 92340,
				"to": 96100
			},
			"text": " Every science writer always compares everything to the atomic bomb dropped on Hiroshima, so"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:36,100",
				"to": "00:01:37,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 96100,
				"to": 97740
			},
			"text": " we may as well get that out of the way."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:37,740",
				"to": "00:01:40,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 97740,
				"to": 100780
			},
			"text": " The lightning bolt would deliver about two atomic bombs' worth of energy to the air"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:40,780",
				"to": "00:01:41,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 100780,
				"to": 101780
			},
			"text": " and ground."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:41,780",
				"to": "00:01:45,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 101780,
				"to": 105980
			},
			"text": " From a more practical standpoint, this is enough energy to power a game console and TV for"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:45,980",
				"to": "00:01:47,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 105980,
				"to": 107620
			},
			"text": " several million years."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:47,620",
				"to": "00:01:51,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 107620,
				"to": 111460
			},
			"text": " Or to put it another way, it could support the U.S.'s electricity consumption for five"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:51,460",
				"to": "00:01:52,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 111460,
				"to": 112460
			},
			"text": " minutes."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:52,460",
				"to": "00:01:55,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 112460,
				"to": 115780
			},
			"text": " The bolt itself would only be as narrow as the center circle of a basketball court, but"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:55,780",
				"to": "00:01:58,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 115780,
				"to": 118740
			},
			"text": " it would leave a crater the size of the entire court."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:58,740",
				"to": "00:02:01,420"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 118740,
				"to": 121420
			},
			"text": " Inside the channel, the air would turn to high-energy plasma."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:01,420",
				"to": "00:02:05,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 121420,
				"to": 125460
			},
			"text": " The light and heat from the bolt would spontaneously ignite surfaces for miles around, the shockwave"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:05,460",
				"to": "00:02:07,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 125460,
				"to": 127620
			},
			"text": " would flatten trees and demolish buildings."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:07,620",
				"to": "00:02:10,500"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 127620,
				"to": 130500
			},
			"text": " All in all, the Hiroshima comparison isn't far off."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:10,500",
				"to": "00:02:13,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 130500,
				"to": 133460
			},
			"text": " You might hope you could collect the energy of the bolt using a lightning rod."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:13,460",
				"to": "00:02:16,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 133460,
				"to": 136940
			},
			"text": " The mechanism by which lightning rods work is actually disputed."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:16,940",
				"to": "00:02:20,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 136940,
				"to": 140900
			},
			"text": " The traditional idea is that they provide a channel to divert current directly to the ground,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:20,900",
				"to": "00:02:24,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 140900,
				"to": 144540
			},
			"text": " while some people claim that they actually ward off lightning strikes by steadily transferring"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:24,540",
				"to": "00:02:28,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 144540,
				"to": 148740
			},
			"text": " charge from the ground to the air, lowering the cloud-to-ground voltage difference and"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:28,740",
				"to": "00:02:30,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 148740,
				"to": 150540
			},
			"text": " reducing the probability of a strike."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:30,540",
				"to": "00:02:33,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 150540,
				"to": 153780
			},
			"text": " Either way, a lightning rod wouldn't keep you safe from Trevor's lightning."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:33,780",
				"to": "00:02:37,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 153780,
				"to": 157980
			},
			"text": " A copper cable a meter in diameter could, in theory, conduct the brief surge of current"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:37,980",
				"to": "00:02:41,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 157980,
				"to": 161740
			},
			"text": " from the bolt without melting, but unfortunately whatever is at the other end of this cable"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:41,740",
				"to": "00:02:45,660"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 161740,
				"to": 165660
			},
			"text": " probably wouldn't conduct electricity nearly as well, and an explosion would disintegrate"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:45,660",
				"to": "00:02:47,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 165660,
				"to": 167980
			},
			"text": " everything nearby all the same."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:47,980",
				"to": "00:02:51,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 167980,
				"to": 171060
			},
			"text": " Gathering all the world's lightning into one place is obviously impractical, but what"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:51,060",
				"to": "00:02:53,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 171060,
				"to": 173780
			},
			"text": " about gathering all the lightning from just one area?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:53,780",
				"to": "00:02:57,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 173780,
				"to": 177620
			},
			"text": " No place on Earth has constant lightning, but there is an area in Venezuela which comes"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:57,620",
				"to": "00:02:58,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 177620,
				"to": 178620
			},
			"text": " close."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:58,620",
				"to": "00:03:02,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 178620,
				"to": 182900
			},
			"text": " Near the southwestern edge of Lake Maracaibo, there's a strange phenomenon - perpetual nighttime"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:02,900",
				"to": "00:03:03,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 182900,
				"to": 183900
			},
			"text": " thunderstorms."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:03,900",
				"to": "00:03:07,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 183900,
				"to": 187900
			},
			"text": " There are two spots, one over the lake and one over the land of the west, where thunderstorms"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:07,900",
				"to": "00:03:09,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 187900,
				"to": 189700
			},
			"text": " form almost every night."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:09,700",
				"to": "00:03:13,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 189700,
				"to": 193540
			},
			"text": " These storms can generate a flash of lightning every two seconds, making Lake Maracaibo the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:13,540",
				"to": "00:03:15,300"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 193540,
				"to": 195300
			},
			"text": " lightning capital of the world."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:15,300",
				"to": "00:03:19,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 195300,
				"to": 199360
			},
			"text": " If you somehow managed to channel all the bolts from a single night of Catatombu thunderstorms"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:19,360",
				"to": "00:03:23,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 199360,
				"to": 203320
			},
			"text": " down through a single lightning rod, and used it to charge a massive capacitor, it would"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:23,320",
				"to": "00:03:27,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 203320,
				"to": 207460
			},
			"text": " store up enough power to run a game console and TV for roughly a century."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:27,460",
				"to": "00:03:31,380"
			},
			"offsets": {
